---
permalink: /next/studio/
title: Studio
description: The people of SMASH, an experience design studio in Stockholm.
section: studio
bodyClass: studio-page
styles:
  - studio.css
---
{#- The studio: its one sentence, the studio at work on a plate (the 12
    columns), its words alone at column 7, then the people. Nothing here
    bleeds: full bleed is kept for thresholds. Media markup is written
    inline: {% image %} renders nothing inside an include or a macro. -#}

<section class="grid page-start" aria-labelledby="studio-title">
  <h1 class="c-1-9 t-large" id="studio-title">A studio of three, working with the makers each piece needs.</h1>
</section>

<div class="st-plate f-plate grid">
  <div class="media c-all" style="--ar: 1.5; --focus: 50% 40%">{% image 'projects/dome-conductor/development.jpg', 'A developer works at a laptop and a monitor showing the dome projection setup, with the orchestra projected in the background.', '(max-width: 719px) 100vw, 94vw', 'eager' %}</div>
</div>

<div class="st-text grid">
  <div class="c-7-12 t-body prose measure">
    <p>We take each piece from the first idea to its last night: the story and the animation, the software, and the controllers and pads people touch. We test on scale models and drone scans, then fit the light to the building on site.</p>
  </div>
</div>

{#- The portraits are drawn larger than their frames (studio.css crops each to
    the set), so their sizes ask for about 1.8 times the frame's width. #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="people-title">
  <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="people-title">People</h2>
  <ul class="grid st-team" role="list">
    {%- for p in team %}
    <li class="st-member" data-person="{{ p.name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}">
      <div class="media">{{ p.picture | replace('(max-width: 720px) 33vw, 22vw', '(max-width: 719px) 180vw, 57vw') | safe }}</div>
      <p class="st-name caption t-body">{{ p.name }}</p>
      <p><a href="mailto:{{ p.email }}">{{ p.email | replace('@', '<wbr>@') | safe }}</a></p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
